Project listing with filtering

Usage: raps admin project [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list          List projects with filtering
  get           Get a project's details
  create        Create a new project
  update        Update an existing project
  archive       Archive a project (sets status to archived)
  create-batch  Create multiple projects in parallel (batch)
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --output <FORMAT>       Output format: table, json, yaml, csv, or plain (default: auto-detect) [possible values: table, json, yaml, csv, plain, ndjson]
      --no-color              Disable colored output
  -q, --quiet                 Print only the result payload (useful with JSON output)
  -v, --verbose               Show verbose output (request summaries)
      --debug                 Show debug output (full trace, secrets redacted)
      --log-file <PATH>       Write log output to PATH instead of the default platform log directory
      --profile               Profile performance (execution time, HTTP network time)
      --non-interactive       Non-interactive mode: fail if prompts would be required
      --yes                   Auto-confirm destructive actions
      --strict                Strict mode for CI: fail on any ambiguity, no silent defaults
      --timeout <SECONDS>     HTTP request timeout in seconds (default: 120, env: RAPS_TIMEOUT)
      --max-retries <N>       Maximum retries for 408/429/5xx responses (default: 3, env: RAPS_MAX_RETRIES). Retries use exponential backoff with jitter and respect Retry-After headers
      --base-delay <SECONDS>  Base delay in seconds for exponential backoff (default: 1, env: RAPS_BASE_DELAY)
      --max-wait <SECONDS>    Maximum wait time in seconds between retries (default: 60, env: RAPS_MAX_WAIT)
      --no-retry              Disable automatic retries (fail immediately on errors)
      --proxy <URL>           HTTP/HTTPS proxy URL (env: RAPS_PROXY), e.g. http://proxy.corp.example.com:8080
      --concurrency <N>       Maximum concurrent operations for bulk commands (default: 5, env: RAPS_CONCURRENCY)
      --no-cache              Disable the download cache
      --cache-dir <PATH>      Custom cache directory (default: platform cache dir)
      --refresh               Ignore cached artifacts and re-download
      --offline               Fail if artifact is not cached (no network requests for downloads)
  -h, --help                  Print help
  -V, --version               Print version
